      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.5 Local Self-Government"
    },
    {
      "id": "m8c85kc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Urban Local Bodies"
    },
    {
      "id": "hdj9gvu",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Municipal Corporations</strong></p>",
            "<p>Municipal Corporations for cities above 3 lakh population; largest – Brihanmumbai Municipal Corporation (BMC/MCGM)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>BMC/MCGM</strong></p>",
            "<p>Richest Municipal Corporation in India; budget larger than many Indian states</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Municipal Councils</strong></p>",
            "<p>Medium-sized towns (below 3 lakh but above certain limits)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Nagar Panchayats</strong></p>",
            "<p>Small towns and transitional areas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Cantonment Boards</strong></p>",
            "<p>Areas under Army Cantonments</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cqun9jw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Rural Local Bodies (Panchayati Raj)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0zgl2al",
      "content": "Maharashtra was among the first states to implement the 73rd Constitutional Amendment for Panchayati Raj. The three-tier system is:"
    },
    {
      "id": "cfoozzq",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Gram Panchayat</strong></p>",
            "<p>Village level; Sarpanch is head; manages village development</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Panchayat Samiti</strong></p>",
            "<p>Block/Taluka level; BDO is administrative head; Sabhapatai is elected head</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Zilla Parishad</strong></p>",
            "<p>District level; CEO is administrative head; Adhyaksha is elected head</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Gram Sabha</strong></p>",
            "<p>All voters in a village; meets twice a year; final decision-making body at grassroots</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Maharashtra ZP Act</strong></p>",
            "<p>Maharashtra Zilla Parishads, Panchayat Samitis, Gram Panchayats and Nagar Panchayats Act, 1961</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Reservation in PRI</strong></p>",
            "<p>50% reservation for women in Maharashtra's Panchayati Raj institutions (implemented 2012)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "f11qb28",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.6 Maharashtra Police"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fcqx1i3",
      "content": "The Maharashtra Police is one of the largest state police forces in India. It operates under the Maharashtra Police Act and is headed by the Director General of Police (DGP)."
    },
    {
      "id": "towz8bp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Maharashtra Police Structure"
    },
    {
      "id": "moizrkq",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Director General of Police (DGP)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Head of Maharashtra Police</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Additional Director General of Police (ADGP)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Second in command / Range heads</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Inspector General of Police (IGP)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Heads each Range / Zone</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Deputy Inspector General (DIG)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Heads a range or special unit</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Superintendent of Police (SP)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Heads a district (non-metro)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Commissioner of Police</strong></p>",
            "<p>Heads a commissionerate (metro area)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Additional SP / Deputy Commissioner</strong></p>",
            "<p>Subdivision heads</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Sub-Inspector (SI)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Entry-level gazetted-equivalent officer for recruits from MPSC</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Assistant Sub-Inspector (ASI)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Promoted from constable cadre</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Police Constable</strong></p>",
            "<p>Entry level through Maharashtra Police Recruitment</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
